"---
title: "Concepts"
description: "Shapes, measuring and units: the ideas the reference pages assume."
kind: "guide"
id: "guide:concepts"
module: "geo"
version: "2.1.0"
canonical: "https://docs.example.com/guides/concepts.html"
---

# ¶ Concepts

[geo](../index.md) › Guides · Every page: [llms.txt](../llms.txt)

*Shapes, measuring and units: the ideas the reference pages assume.*

Three ideas carry the whole library: a closed set of shapes, pure functions that measure them, and one unit of length. Each section below links to the declarations it describes.

## Shapes

Every shape implements the sealed interface [\`Shape\`](../com/example/geo/Shape.md). Two classes implement it:

- [\`Circle\`](../com/example/geo/Circle.md), a record of a radius and an optional label.
  
  - Create one with [\`Circle.of(double)\`](../com/example/geo/Circle.md#of%28double%29).
  - Its [\`area()\`](../com/example/geo/Circle.md#area%28%29) is \`π r²\`.
- [\`Polygon\`](../com/example/geo/Polygon.md), a regular polygon built from its sides.
  
  - It extends [\`AbstractShape\`](../com/example/geo/AbstractShape.md), which adds [\`perimeter()\`](../com/example/geo/AbstractShape.md#perimeter%28%29).
  - It is not sealed: [Custom shapes](advanced/custom-shapes.md) shows how to extend it.

> [!NOTE]
> Because the hierarchy is sealed, a \`switch\` over a shape needs no \`default\` branch, and the compiler tells you when a new shape appears.

### Example

\`\`\`java
String describe(Shape shape) {
    return switch (shape) {
        case Circle c -> "circle of radius " + c.radius();
        case Polygon p -> "polygon with perimeter " + p.perimeter();
    };
}
\`\`\`

## Measuring

[\`Shapes\`](../com/example/geo/Shapes.md) holds the operations. They are pure: none modifies its arguments. \`area\` is overloaded, so the compiler picks [\`area(Circle)\`](../com/example/geo/Shapes.md#area%28com.example.geo.Circle%29) or [\`area(Polygon)\`](../com/example/geo/Shapes.md#area%28com.example.geo.Polygon%29) from the argument's static type.

1. Build the shapes.
2. Measure each one, or sum them with [\`total(Shape...)\`](../com/example/geo/Shapes.md#total%28com.example.geo.Shape...%29).
3. Compare the results: shapes order by area.

> [!TIP]
> **Collecting shapes**
>
> To collect shapes as you go, use [\`Shapes.Builder\`](../com/example/geo/Shapes.Builder.md) with the options of its nested enum [\`Shapes.Builder.Option\`](../com/example/geo/Shapes.Builder.Option.md), such as [\`SORTED\`](../com/example/geo/Shapes.Builder.Option.md#SORTED).

### Example

\`\`\`java
double small = Shapes.area(Circle.of(1));
double large = Shapes.area(new Polygon(4, 4, 4, 4));
assert small < large;
\`\`\`

## Units

Every length is in meters, and every area in square meters. [\`Units\`](../com/example/geo/Units.md) converts other units at the edges of a program:

Units of length

| Unit | Meters per unit | Status |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [\`Units.METERS\`](../com/example/geo/Units.md#METERS) | \`1.0\` | The base unit |
| [\`Units.FEET\`](../com/example/geo/Units.md#FEET) | \`0.3048\` | Deprecated since 1.2 |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Methods take and return meters. Convert once, when a value enters the program, with [\`toMeters(double)\`](../com/example/geo/Units.md#toMeters%28double%29).

> [!WARNING]
> **Round trips lose precision**
>
> Converting back and forth between units loses precision. Keep lengths in meters until you show them.

## Parsing

[\`Shapes.parse\`](../com/example/geo/Shapes.md#parse%28java.lang.String%29) reads the text form of one shape. The [text format guide](advanced/text-format.md#grammar) has the grammar.

> [!CAUTION]
> The text form is not stable across releases. Store shapes some other way, and never parse text you do not trust without a size limit.

## Threads

> **⚠︎ API note**
>
> Every method of [\`Shapes\`](../com/example/geo/Shapes.md) is safe to call from several threads at once.

> **☑︎ Implementation requirements**
>
> A subclass of [\`Polygon\`](../com/example/geo/Polygon.md) must keep \`area()\` free of side effects, so that callers may cache it.

> **✎ Implementation note**
>
> The library keeps no caches and allocates only the results it returns.

## Further reading

- [Polygon](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polygon) on Wikipedia.
- [Classes to replace](migrating-from-1x.md#classes-to-replace), in the migration guide.
- \`Ellipse\` is planned for a later release. This model does not contain it, so the link renders as plain text.
- Recipes is a guide that does not exist yet, so this link renders as plain text too.

---

Previous: [Getting started](getting-started.md)  
Next: [Migrating from 1.x](migrating-from-1x.md)
"
`;

exports[`outputs guide page snapshots, HTML and Markdown: guides/advanced/text-format.md 1`] = `
"---
title: "The text format"
description: "The grammar Shapes.parse reads, and how to read files of shapes."
kind: "guide"
id: "guide:advanced/text-format"
module: "geo"
version: "2.1.0"
canonical: "https://docs.example.com/guides/advanced/text-format.html"
---

# ¶ The text format

[geo](../../index.md) › Advanced · Every page: [llms.txt](../../llms.txt)

*The grammar \`Shapes.parse\` reads, and how to read files of shapes.*

Shapes have a one-line text form, for logs and test fixtures. [\`Shapes.parse\`](../../com/example/geo/Shapes.md#parse%28java.lang.String%29) reads one; [\`ShapeReader\`](../../com/example/geo/io/ShapeReader.md) reads a stream of them.

## Grammar

\`\`\`text
shape   = circle | polygon
circle  = "circle" number
polygon = "polygon" number number number { number }
number  = digit { digit } [ "." digit { digit } ]
\`\`\`

Numbers are lengths in meters. Blank lines and lines starting with \`#\` are skipped.

## Reading files

[\`read(InputStream)\`](../../com/example/geo/io/ShapeReader.md#read%28java.io.InputStream%29) reads UTF-8 text; the [\`read(Reader, Charset)\`](../../com/example/geo/io/ShapeReader.md#read%28java.io.Reader,java.nio.charset.Charset%29) overload reads text you have already decoded.

\`\`\`java
try (var in = Files.newInputStream(Path.of("shapes.txt"))) {
    List<Shape> shapes = ShapeReader.read(in);
}
\`\`\`

> [!WARNING]
> A malformed line throws [\`GeometryException\`](../../com/example/geo/GeometryException.md) and stops the read. Validate files from users before you read them.

---

Previous: [Custom shapes](custom-shapes.md)
"
`;

