de><small>index of every page</small></a></li><li><a href="../llms-full.txt"><code>llms-full.txt</code><small>the whole reference</small></a></li><li><a href="../api.json"><code>api.json</code><small>the model</small></a></li><li class="formats-sep"><a href="https://claude.ai/new?q=Read%20https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.example.com%2Fguides%2Fgetting-started.md%20so%20that%20I%20can%20ask%20questions%20about%20Getting%20started%20(geo%202.1.0)." rel="noopener"><span>Open in Claude</span><small>↗︎</small></a></li><li><a href="https://chatgpt.com/?q=Read%20https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.example.com%2Fguides%2Fgetting-started.md%20so%20that%20I%20can%20ask%20questions%20about%20Getting%20started%20(geo%202.1.0)." rel="noopener"><span>Open in ChatGPT</span><small>↗︎</small></a></li></ul></details></div></div><article class="guide" data-guide-id="guide:getting-started" data-reading-progress="true"><header class="page-head guide-head"><p class="guide-kicker">Guide</p><h1>Getting started</h1><p class="lede guide-summary">Add geo to a build and measure a first shape.</p><p class="page-meta"></p></header><div id="guide-body" class="prose guide-body"><div class="guide-intro"><p>geo measures plane shapes: circles, polygons and shapes you build from them. This guide adds it to a build and runs a first program.</p></div><section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="install"><h2 id="install" class="doc-heading guide-heading">Install<a class="heading-anchor" href="getting-started.html#install" aria-label="Link to this section"><span aria-hidden="true">#</span></a></h2><p>geo needs Java 21 or later. With Gradle, add the dependency to <code>build.gradle.kts</code>:</p><div class="code-block"><pre data-lang="kotlin"><code>dependencies {
    <span class="hl-f">implementation</span>(<span class="hl-s">&quot;com.example:geo:2.1.0&quot;</span>)
}</code></pre><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="true" hidden aria-label="Copy code" title="Copy code">Copy</button></div><p>With Maven, add it to <code>pom.xml</code>:</p><div class="code-block"><pre data-lang="xml"><code><span class="hl-k">&lt;dependency></span>
  <span class="hl-k">&lt;groupId></span>com.example<span class="hl-k">&lt;/groupId></span>
  <span class="hl-k">&lt;artifactId></span>geo<span class="hl-k">&lt;/artifactId></span>
  <span class="hl-k">&lt;version></span>2.1.0<span class="hl-k">&lt;/version></span>
<span class="hl-k">&lt;/dependency></span></code></pre><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="true" hidden aria-label="Copy code" title="Copy code">Copy</button></div><p>On the module path, require the module:</p><div class="code-block"><pre data-lang="java"><code><span class="hl-k">module</span> my.app {
    <span class="hl-k">requires</span> com.example.geo;
}</code></pre><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="true" hidden aria-label="Copy code" title="Copy code">Copy</button></div></section><section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="your-first-shape"><h2 id="your-first-shape" class="doc-heading guide-heading">Your first shape<a class="heading-anchor" href="getting-started.html#your-first-shape" aria-label="Link to this section"><span aria-hidden="true">#</span></a></h2><p>Create shapes with <a href="../com/example/geo/Circle.html#of(double)"><code>Circle.of</code></a> and the <a href="../com/example/geo/Polygon.html#%3Cinit%3E(double...)"><code>Polygon</code></a> constructor, then measure them with <a href="../com/example/geo/Shapes.html"><code>Shapes</code></a>:</p><div class="code-block"><pre data-lang="java"><code><span class="hl-k">import</span> com.example.geo.*;

<span class="hl-k">class</span> <span class="hl-t">First</span> {
    <span class="hl-k">public</span> <span class="hl-k">static</span> <span class="hl-k">void</span> <span class="hl-f">main</span>(<span class="hl-t">String</span>[] args) {
        <span class="hl-t">Shape</span> circle = <span class="hl-t">Circle</span>.<span class="hl-f">of</span>(<span class="hl-n">2</span>);
        <span class="hl-t">Shape</span> triangle = <span class="hl-k">new</span> <span class="hl-t">Polygon</span>(<span class="hl-n">3</span>, <span class="hl-n">3</span>, <span class="hl-n">3</span>);
        <span class="hl-t">System</span>.out.<span class="hl-f">printf</span>(<span class="hl-s">&quot;total area: %.2f m²%n&quot;</span>, <span class="hl-t">Shapes</span>.<span class="hl-f">total</span>(circle, triangle));
    }
}</code></pre><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy="true" hidden aria-label="Copy code" title="Copy code">Copy</button></div><div class="callout callout-tip" role="note"><span class="callout-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16"><path d="M5.6 10.4a4 4 0 1 1 4.8 0c-.4.3-.6.7-.6 1.2H6.2c0-.5-.2-.9-.6-1.2z"></path><path d="M6.5 13.6h3"></path></svg></span><div class="callout-body"><p class="callout-label">Tip</p><p>Every length is in meters. To work in other units, see <a href="concepts.html#units">Units</a> in the concepts guide.</p></div></div></section><section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="next-steps"><h2 id="next-steps" class="doc-heading guide-heading">Next steps<a class="heading-anchor" href="getting-started.html#next-steps" aria-label="Link to this section"><span aria-hidden="true">#</span></a></h2><ul><li><p><a href="concepts.html">Concepts</a> explains shapes, measuring and units.</p></li><li><p><a href="migrating-from-1x.html">Migrating from 1.x</a> lists what changed in 2.0.</p></li><li><p>The <a href="../com/example/geo/index.html"><code>com.example.geo</code></a> package is the reference for everything above.</p></li></ul></section></div><nav class="guide-pager" aria-label="Previous and next guides"><a class="guide-pager-link guide-next" rel="next" href="concepts.html"><span class="guide-pager-dir">Next</span><span class="guide-pager-title">Concepts</span></a></nav></article></main><footer class="footer"><p><a href="getting-started.md">This page as Markdown</a>, <a href="../llms.txt">llms.txt</a>, <a href="../api.json">api.json</a><span data-js-only="true">, <button type="button" class="footer-keys" data-keys-open="true" aria-keyshortcuts="?">Keyboard shortcuts</button></span></p></footer></div></body></html>
